 "intro_html": "Malai means cream. Two of Swasthi’s recipes put together: her <b>malai (reshmi) kabab</b> for the tikka — chicken in cream, yogurt, cheese and ground almonds and cashews, charred in a very hot oven — and her <b>malai chicken gravy</b>: onion, ginger and garlic sautéed pale, ground with cashews and milk and simmered with whole spices. Mild, creamy and gently spiced, like a butter chicken without the tomato. The gravy is naturally ivory; a pinch of turmeric makes it the yellow you remember (optional — see notes). Make the gravy while the tikka marinates or grills.",
