 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Swasthi’s malai chicken marinates plain chicken in spiced yogurt and pan-fries it before it goes into the gravy.</li><li>Here her <b>malai tikka</b> takes its place — grilled, charred and creamy — the way restaurants serve malai tikka masala.</li><li>The tikka amounts are her <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"250\" data-s=\"0\">250 g</span> kabab card <b>doubled</b> to match the gravy’s <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"500\" data-s=\"0\">500 g</span>, and only the half of her ghee that tempers the spices is used (the other half fried her chicken).</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Two recipes put together"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Both of Swasthi’s recipes come out ivory-white.</li><li>For the yellow you remember, add a pinch of turmeric to the gravy with the other spices (or a few saffron strands soaked in a teaspoon of warm milk).</li><li>That’s an addition, not part of her recipes.</li><li>Keep the onions pale and use garam masala without chilli, or the gravy turns brown or orange.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Yellow colour (optional)"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Swasthi’s kabab card calls for almond meal; ground almonds and cashews with the yogurt is her own alternative.</li><li><b>Untested:</b> all cashews (about 40) should work the same and taste a little sweeter.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Cashews and almonds in the tikka"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>From Sinfully Spicy’s malai tikka.</li><li><b>Air fryer:</b> <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"200\" data-s=\"0\">200 °C</span> for 16–18 min.</li><li><b>Pan:</b> heat a cast-iron or grill pan over medium-high (not smoking), brush with ghee or butter, cook in one layer 3–4 min, brushing with ghee, then flip and cook until lightly charred.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Pan or air fryer for the tikka"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Chicken is safe at <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"74\" data-s=\"0\">74 °C</span></b> in the centre.</li><li>Cut the biggest piece open if unsure.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Is it cooked?"
  }
 ],
